    <md:title>1.11.4: Identifying the Features of a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e4d53868-930e-4999-b222-337b96027e4f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>For numbers 1 – 3, consider the equation \(1.5x + 4.5y = 18\).</para>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>If we graph the equation, what is the slope of the graph?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The slope is \( -\frac{1}{3} \). Rearranging the equation to isolate \( y \) gives \( y=-\frac{1}{3}x\ +\ 4 \).</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Where does the graph intersect the \( y \)-axis?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>The graph intersects the \(y\)-axis at \( (0, 4) \). The \( 4 \) in \( y=-\frac{1}{3}x+4 \) tells us where the graph crosses the \( y \)-axis.</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Where does it intersect the \( x \)-axis?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>The graph intersects the \(x\)-axis at \((12,0)\). Substituting 0 for \(y\) in the original equation and solving for \(x\) gives \(x=12\).</para>
  </solution></exercise></section>
</content>
